# Known bug: a permanent entering is judged by its own card, not with other objects' type-changing effects, so Humility does not strip the "as this enters" of a land Life and Limb would make a creature (CR 614.12; KI-52).
# Overgrown Tomb (Land - Swamp Forest: "As this land enters, you may pay 2 life. If you don't, it enters tapped.") played
# under Life and Limb and Humility. CR 614.12: its replacement effects are judged on it as it would exist on the
# battlefield, "taking into account ... continuous effects that already exist and would apply to the permanent". There it
# is a Forest, so Life and Limb makes it a 1/1 green Saproling creature (layer 4), and Humility takes all its abilities
# (layer 6) - the "as this enters" among them. So Bot1 is asked nothing, pays no life and the Tomb enters untapped (a
# creature that lost its mana abilities, it can't tap for mana anyway).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Life and Limb
Humility
Plains
Overgrown Tomb
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Life and Limb.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Humility.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Overgrown Tomb.Play
! Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Overgrown Tomb.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Overgrown Tomb.Types = Land; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Overgrown Tomb.Power = 1
